[nH+]cc2c1","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-018345","value":"5.9","numeric":5.9}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-018346","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"KP1019","Cell_line":"MCF-10A","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":">100","IC50_Dark_value":100,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1021/acs.organomet.3c00394","Year":2024,"Counterion":"c1ccc2[nH][nH+]cc2c1","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-018346","value":">100","numeric":100}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"KP1019","value":-0.4,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/elps.201700443","year":2018,"counterion":"c1ccc2[nH][nH+]cc2c1","record_id":"MLDB-000213","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"The shake flask procedure outlined previously 28, 46 was followed for the determination of solubility and log P values. A saturated solution of complex was suspended in H2O (pre-saturated with n-octanol) and shaken for 4 days on an orbital shaker. The solution was centrifuged for 5 min at 2000 rpm prior to aqueous aliquots being collected for total Ru concentration analysis, and partition experiments with n-octanol (pre-saturated with H2O) at three ratios (2:1, 1:1, and 0.5:1). After 30 min incubation time on an orbital shaker, the samples were shaken by hand for an additional 5 min and were then centrifuged at 10 000 rpm for 5 min. The aqueous layer was collected with a syringe and diluted 1:100 in 5% HNO3. The ruthenium content was measured via direct infusion through an ASX-500 autosampler (CETAC technologies) in a Serie SuSi laminar flow hood (SPECTEC) into an Agilent 7700 ICP-MS, equipped with a MicroMist nebulizer and a Scott double pass spray chamber. All analysis were carried out in triplicate unless otherwise specified."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"KP1019","value":-0.6,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1007/s10534-019-00210-7","year":2019,"counterion":"c1ccc2[nH][nH+]cc2c1","record_id":"MLDB-004361","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol–water partition coefficients were determined by a modified shake-flask method (Cirri et al. 2017, Marzo et al. 2017). Water (250 mL, distilled after Milli-Q purification) and n-octanol (250 mL) were shaken together for 72 h to allow saturation of both phases in a 500 mL flask. The suspension was allowed to separate at least for one week in the dark. A solution of the complexes was prepared using the water phase (3 × 10-3 M) and an equal volume of octanol was added. Biphasic solutions were mixed for ten minutes and then centrifuged at 25 °C with an MPW-260R centrifuge equipped with a 11,746 rotor for 5 min at 6000 rpm to allow separation. Concentrations in both phases were determined through UV–Vis or ICP-AES spectroscopy depending on the properties of each complex. Reported logP values are defined as log10([complex]oct/[complex]wat). Final values were reported as mean of three determinations."}],"related_salts":[{"id":"OBMD000259","name":"BOLD-100"}],"melting_points":[{"temperature_c":"248","event":"Decomposition reported","Counterion":"c1ccc2[nH][nH+]cc2c1","source":"10.1155/mbd.1996.243","source_page":"p. 245, Complex Syntheses","notes":"Compound 1, indazolium KP1019. Source reports decomp. at 248 °C.","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/mbd.1996.243"}]}